# Items-are-real contract allowlist (tickets 175 + 429).
#
# Format: `<file> <ticket-id> [# rationale]`
#   * `<file>` — path relative to repo root (whole-file allowlist)
#   * `<ticket-id>` — ticket that authorizes the bypass / tracks the
#     follow-on promotion
#   * Comment-only lines start with `#`. Trailing comments allowed.
#
# Two classes of entry:
#
#   175 — `stored.remove + despawn` patterns that are genuinely not a
#         transfer (consumption, cat-death cleanup, world-teardown,
#         entity-replacement that's part of an in-place transformation).
#
#   429 — Inventory-mutation or Item:: spawn sites pending promotion to
#         a first-class `ItemSource` impl. The ticket id should name the
#         follow-on promotion ticket; whole-file allowlisting trades
#         coverage on that file for lint-fail-free landing of the
#         in-scope work.
#
# The contract modules (`src/components/item_transfer.rs`,
# `src/components/item_gate.rs` + submodules, `src/components/items.rs`,
# `src/components/magic.rs`) and the resolver layer (`src/steps/**`),
# test harnesses (`src/scenarios/**`, `src/world_gen/**`,
# `src/rendering/**`), and `#[cfg(test)] mod tests {` blocks inside
# otherwise-prod files are auto-skipped by the lint and don't need
# allowlist entries.

# 175: consumption (despawn-as-real-world-effect), not transfer.
src/steps/disposition/eat_at_stores.rs 175  # cat eats food from Stores; the despawn IS the consumption
src/systems/prey.rs 175                     # wild animal raids Stores; despawn is the food being eaten

# 482 retired the 429-deferred entries — PreservationOutputSource /
# HarvestCarcassSource / ForageIngredientSource now dispatch the three
# previously-allowlisted call sites. No active 429 follow-on entries
# remain.
